  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>First heterolytic&nbsp;fission of iodine will take place and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;will attack at double bond site. Then oxygen of carboxylic acid will attack on the carbocation, forming a cyclic ring. In last step elimination reaction will take place in presence of heat and Py.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0020_86111499f342.png\" style=\"width: 526px; height: 250px;\" /></p></blockquote>"
